# Build context: ./frontend
#
# The image installs from package-lock.json and builds with Vite. What is here
# is either rebuilt inside the image or cannot run in it.

# Recipe and context filter: read by the daemon before the build, never copied.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# The reason this file exists. node_modules holds binaries linked against
# darwin/arm64 (esbuild, rollup); copied into a linux image they fail at exec.
# `npm ci` installs the right ones. It is also the bulk of the context.
**/node_modules

# Built inside the image by `npm run build`. A dist/ from the host would be
# copied over the fresh build, and the container would serve stale assets.
dist
dist-ssr

# Never in an image, whatever it holds. The port is the only thing the
# environment decides and the backend owns that; nothing here is configured
# through a file.
.env
.env.*

# Coverage report. The numbers ship in the README, the artefact does not.
coverage

# Logs.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor, VCS and OS noise.
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Scaffold docs: not part of a production build, and every edit would bust the
# cache of the COPY layer underneath.
README.md

# eslint.config.js and tsconfig*.json stay in the context: `npm run build` runs
# `tsc -b` first, so the type config is part of the build, and a lint or test
# stage reads the rest. The test files, once they exist, stay for the same
# reason.
